; opencode-egress-macos.sb — the #1644 macOS operator recipe.
;
; A `sandbox-exec` profile denying every outbound network connection except
; loopback, for an operator to repeat the Linux CI job's egress check by hand
; against a real LM Studio/Ollama during #1659. The Linux network-namespace +
; strace job (.github/workflows/opencode-egress.yml) is the gating evidence
; for this issue; this profile is a documented, operator-run tool, not a CI
; job of its own.
;
; Usage:
;   sandbox-exec -f scripts/opencode-egress-macos.sb curl -sS https://example.com
;     must FAIL (denied outbound to a non-loopback host).
;   sandbox-exec -f scripts/opencode-egress-macos.sb curl 127.0.0.1:<stub-port>/v1/models
;     must SUCCEED (loopback is allowed).
;
; Run the real check under this profile the same way:
;   sandbox-exec -f scripts/opencode-egress-macos.sb opencode run --format json ...
;
; Observe every denied attempt live, in a second terminal, while the command
; above runs:
;   log stream --predicate 'eventMessage CONTAINS "deny" AND eventMessage CONTAINS "network"'
;
; Declaring one additional LAN endpoint for the manual #1659 repeat (a
; declared, operator-run model server on the local network — see ADR-022's
; "Endpoints" amendment): append one more allow rule naming exactly that
; host and port, e.g.
;   (allow network-outbound (remote ip "192.168.1.42:1234"))
; Add at most one such rule per repeat, matching the endpoint under test, and
; keep the `log stream` predicate above running so any OTHER denied attempt
; is still visible. This profile itself declares none — an operator adds the
; single line for their own repeat and discards the edit afterward, it is
; not committed as part of this profile.

(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network-outbound)
(allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:*"))
